	<h1 class="title mb-2">Principal Assumptions and Sources</h1>
	<p class="text-accent mb-8">The Hidden Costs of Solar Delay, August 6, 2026 version</p>

	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
		<p>
			This page carries the assumptions and sources behind
			<a href="/presentation/">John Pepi's narrated presentation</a> for the Western Massachusetts
			Clean Energy Network. The parameters and the mitigation rate derivation are John's. The group
			maintains this page and updates it as sources are added. Last updated August 10, 2026, for
			the August 6 revision of the talk.
		</p>
		<p>
			The August 6 revision changed several inputs. The grid emissions factor now comes from the
			EPA AVERT avoided emission rates rather than a UNFCCC combined margin calculation. Forest
			sequestration drops from 2 to 1.5 metric tons per acre per year. Curtailment rises over time
			instead of sitting at a flat lifetime rate. Grid losses are no longer charged against solar
			output. The net effect raises the mitigation rate from 600 to 748 pounds of CO2e per
			megawatt-hour and raises the forest acreage in the shortfall scenario from 88,000 to 131,000.
		</p>

